  {
   "id": "p58-rb1-e05",
   "page": 58,
   "box": 1,
   "kind_hint": "management",
   "section": "Manage and refer urgently:",
   "section_y": 121.2,
   "indent": 1,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "If shock/SBP < 80, give sodium chloride 0.9% 1L IV rapidly, repeat until systolic BP > 80. Continue 1L 6 hourly. Stop if breathing worsens. Refer same day.",
   "bbox": [
    51.4,
    131.4,
    631.3,
    142.2
   ],
   "key": "p58-30f91a10"
  },
  {
   "id": "p58-out-e01",
   "page": 58,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "DIARRHOEA",
   "bbox": [
    370.9,
    48.7,
    471.0,
    71.0
   ],
   "key": "p58-6f0cc57f"
  },
  {
   "id": "p58-out-e02",
   "page": 58,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "1If SBP < 80, pulse ≥ 100, respiratory rate > 30, confusion/restlessness, weakness, shock likely. 2Maximum dose: 10mg (34-39kg), 12mg (40-46kg), 14mg (47-53kg), 16mg (≥ 54kg). 3Give sachets of ORS and advise on home ORS solution: add 8 teaspoons of sugar and half a teaspoon of salt to 1L of boiled water. 4Advise no alcohol until 48 hours after last dose of metronidazole.",
   "bbox": [
    34.0,
    535.3,
    806.8,
    551.8
   ],
   "key": "p58-efbc6ba3"
  },
  {
   "id": "p58-out-e03",
   "page": 58,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Approach to the patient with diarrhoea not needing urgent attention • Confirm patient has diarrhoea: ≥ 3 loose stools/day. • If thirst, dry mouth or poor skin turgor, dehydration likely. Give oral rehydration solution and observe: encourage small frequent sips. Aim for 1-2L in first 2 hours. If vomits, give single dose metoclopramide 10mg orally/IM/IV, wait 10 minutes and try again more slowly. • If unable to drink or no better after 2 hours, give sodium chloride 0.9% 500mL IV over 30 minutes and refer. • If history of prolonged constipation followed by watery stool, overflow diarrhoea likely 60. • Ask about duration of diarrhoea:",
   "bbox": [
    51.0,
    155.8,
    755.3,
    227.0
   ],
   "key": "p58-f18ab8d0"
  },
  {
   "id": "p58-out-e04",
   "page": 58,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Diarrhoea ≤ 2 weeks",
   "bbox": [
    206.3,
    239.2,
    281.2,
    249.4
   ],
   "key": "p58-7c5796f3"
  },
  {
