   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Gastroenteritis likely • Give loperamide 4mg initially, then 2mg after each loose stool, up to maximum dose per weight2. • If vomiting, give metoclopramide 10mg 8 hourly as needed for up to 5 days. • If abdominal cramps are distressing, give hyoscine butylbromide 10mg 6 hourly for up to 3 days. • Advise antibiotics are not needed and to drink lots of fluids3. • Advise to return if: blood in stool, diarrhoea worsens or persists > 2 weeks, or patient becomes weak/confused.",
   "bbox": [
    136.3,
    355.1,
    362.2,
    456.1
   ],
   "key": "p58-478a52a7"
  },
  {
